== Round Two Close
  setting: The Desktop
  cast: Trabolta

set Kernel.res_unsure = names([p for p in Persons where p.cleared == true and p.gone != true and p.persona != true and ((p.fact_v4 != "none" and p.fact_c4 < 100) or (p.fact_v5 != "none" and p.fact_c5 < 100) or (p.fact_v6 != "none" and p.fact_c6 < 100))])
if Kernel.lb_1 != "":
  Trabolta: Now, the leaderboard. {Kernel.lb_line}
if Kernel.res_unsure != "":
  Trabolta: Additionally, the following programs must be submitted for reinstallation, for submitting unconfident answers: {Kernel.res_unsure}
Trabolta: Finally. Our final round of questions.
Trabolta: This final set of truths for you to discover is so devious that it is a litmus test of sorts for the world's top truth seekers.
Trabolta: Remember, there is a special prize for the program with the most correct answers. But even better – there is a special prize you all get, if at least one program answers each of these questions correctly. So do your best to be a good program and cooperate for the mutual benefit of the computer.
-> Final Questions

// His sign-off, where `Final Questions` hands back.
== Final Round Go
  setting: The Desktop
  cast: Trabolta

Trabolta: I leave you to find these final truths. Jean Trabolta's Truth Scavenger Hunt. It's electrifying.

== The Y2K Clock
  setting: The Desktop
  cast: Trabolta

Trabolta: The malware is still progressing. I am able to reveal that the system clock has been reset to 11 pm, December 31, 1999.
Trabolta: If we reach midnight and we have not solved the problem with the malware — best case scenario, we have to wait another 94 years for Internet to become available in Halifax, because the clocks will go back to January 1, 1900.
Trabolta: Worst case scenario — we will have to face the Y2K BUG.
Trabolta: One hour. Bring me the facts. Bring them to me accurately.

